        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.20.12) found new features shipping in Firefox 158 beta which was released last week. Currently, the collector covers about 90% of BCD, so the following list might not be exhaustive. Also, if a feature is in Nightly/behind flags, it is not considered here. If a feature is missing, one reason can be that the IDL is not yet in a specification or in webref.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 158 stable releases on October 13, 2026. This PR needs to be merged before/with the BCD release on October 8, 2026.</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With this PR, BCD will consider the following features as shipping in Firefox 158:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>api.Notification.navigate</li>\n<li>api.PerformanceResourceTiming.deliveryType</li>\n<li>api.Sanitizer.setJavascriptURLs (<a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2068934\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2068934</a>)</li>\n<li>api.WebTransport.supportsReliableOnly_static (<a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2007783\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2007783</a>)</li>\n<li>css.types.calc.typed_division_produces_unitless_number</li>\n<li>css.types.sign.typed_division_produces_unitless_number</li>\n<li>webdriver.bidi.browsingContext.captureScreenshot.imageSize_parameter</li>\n<li>webdriver.bidi.browsingContext.startScreencast.destinationFolder_parameter</li>\n<li>webextensions.api.runtime.getVersion</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See also <a href=\"https://www.firefox.com/en-US/firefox/158.0beta/releasenotes/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.firefox.com/en-US/firefox/158.0beta/releasenotes/</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30755",
            "title": "Updates for Firefox 158 beta",
            "date_modified": "2026-10-05T15:02:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-10-05T15:00:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.20.12) found new features shipping in Chromium 156 beta which was released last week. Currently, the collector covers about 90% of BCD, so the following list might not be exhaustive. Also, if a feature is in Canary/behind flags, it is not considered here. If a feature is missing, one reason can be that the IDL is not yet in a specification or in webref.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 156 stable releases on October 20, 2026. This PR needs to be merged before/with the BCD release on October 15, 2026.</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With this PR, BCD will consider the following features as shipping in Chromium 156:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>css.properties.scroll-snap-type.pair</strong> (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5124378896498688\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5124378896498688</a>)</li>\n<li>css.selectors.navigation-source (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6327898878377984\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6327898878377984</a>)</li>\n<li>css.types.random (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5324559251275776\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5324559251275776</a>)</li>\n<li>css.types.random.dashed-ident</li>\n<li>css.types.random.step</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See also <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/release-notes/156\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/release-notes/156</a></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>WebRTC diagnostic logging might be shipping, too. Maybe an argument to get the spec into webref after all, <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"909474460\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/305\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/browser-specs/issues/305/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/305\">w3c/browser-specs#305</a></li>\n<li>Daniel has <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5528855381\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30604\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30604/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30604\">#30604</a> for <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5214647044145152\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5214647044145152</a></li>\n<li>Unsure about media pseudos. Collector says no.</li>\n</ul>",
