            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83347420?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29241.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4064318473\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29241\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29241/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29241\">#29241</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Following the guidance in the issue, this adds a <code class=\"notranslate\">vertical_oriented_table_cells</code> sub-feature to <code class=\"notranslate\">css.properties.writing-mode</code>, mirroring the existing <code class=\"notranslate\">vertical_oriented_form_controls</code> sub-feature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Data and sources:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Chrome 92</strong>: verified by testing in the issue; tracking bug referenced via <code class=\"notranslate\">impl_url</code> (<a href=\"https://crbug.com/40183612\" rel=\"nofollow\">crbug.com/40183612</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>Firefox 47</strong>: supports vertical table cells, but rendering is not always correct (see screenshot in the issue), so it is marked as <code class=\"notranslate\">partial_implementation</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Safari 17.4</strong>: marked as <code class=\"notranslate\">partial_implementation</code>. The change enabling vertical writing modes for table cells (<a href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/0d695812f5b0daef531a9760903457364d2265ff\">WebKit commit 0d69581</a>) shipped in the WebKit 618.1.10 branch (Safari 17.4), but the follow-up fix was reverted in <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=266941\" rel=\"nofollow\">bug 266941</a> and the tracking bug <a href=\"https://webkit.org/b/266928\" rel=\"nofollow\">266928</a> is still open, so support remains incomplete. The note on the entry explains that vertical writing modes were not applied to <code class=\"notranslate\">th</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">td</code> elements before Safari 17.4, as requested in the issue.</li>\n<li>All other browsers use <code class=\"notranslate\">mirror</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Questions for reviewers:</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Should Firefox's <code class=\"notranslate\">partial_implementation</code> flag start at 47, or is there a later version where rendering is correct?</li>\n<li>The issue title says \"iOS &lt; 17\", but based on the WebKit commit history, 17.4 seems to be the first version with any (partial) support — Safari iOS therefore mirrors 17.4.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Release note</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>CSS: Added <code class=\"notranslate\">vertical_oriented_table_cells</code> subfeature to <code class=\"notranslate\">writing-mode</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30702",
            "title": "Add vertically-oriented table cells sub-feature to writing-mode",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-29T22:43:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-29T15:57:20.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "CloaRK",
                "url": "https://github.com/CloaRK"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">pseudo()</code> method of <code class=\"notranslate\">Element</code> objects has varying support for different values. I've tried to capture this here.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The behavior here is a the consequence of a spec change, resolved in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4261800498\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13804\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13804/hovercard?comment_id=4297936996&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13804#issuecomment-4297936996\">w3c/csswg-drafts#13804 (comment)</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I didn't actually test this but I feel reasonably confident given <a href=\"https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/c1e61b0aebf0c03d81690332f077d14da39efe09\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/c1e61b0aebf0c03d81690332f077d14da39efe09</a> and <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6516055192240128\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6516055192240128</a>.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5336284266\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4306\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4306/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4306\">web-platform-dx/web-features#4306</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30700",
            "title": "Add subfeatures for `api.Element.pseudo` parameter values",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-29T13:25:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-29T13:24:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45960703?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/c9w5uH3eSuo/m/oG9HX5UfCQAJ\" rel=\"nofollow\">This message from intent to remove sent on Sept 28:</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We landed the required code in M156. The fenced frame element and window.fence are now stubs starting in M156. We will start the experiment to remove the stubs in M157. Thanks!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6366274495053824\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chrome Status entry (updated recently)</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This Chromium commit removed Fenced Frames API:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8144621\" rel=\"nofollow\">CL 8144621</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/55fa5f273aed691fbe11a449cabf1943fb284f74\">This commit on GitHub</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/fenced-frame/fenced-frame-stub.https.html\">WPT test for stubs</a> - this explains all the <code class=\"notranslate\">notes</code> I added.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a direct follow-up to my earlier PR deprecating Fenced Frame API <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5161427314\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30242\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30242/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30242\">#30242</a><br>\nThis is relaed to Shared Storeage API PR I created <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5568937249\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30659\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30659/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30659\">#30659</a></p>\n\n",
